    ]
  },
  "inspection_run": {
    "__comment": "[VOID SCHEMA — the DENOMINATOR] One row = one scan that HAPPENED. It exists so that 'no void rows' can be told apart from 'never scanned'; a void_yn column on bonding_log cannot tell those apart and both read false (DEFECT_SCHEMA_PROPOSAL §1). Yield needs a denominator: '3 voids' means nothing without 'out of how many scans'. | KEY = (method, base_wafer_id, base_x, base_y, stack_gate, observed_at). A scan is 'this method looked at this package layer at this instant', and a package cannot be in two machines at once, so that tuple is unique by physics. recipe_id/eqp_id are RECORDED BUT NOT KEY MATERIAL, deliberately: a re-delivered file that corrects a typo'd recipe must UPDATE the run, not mint a second one and orphan its voids. 🔴 The cost, named: if a source's observed_at is coarser than the re-scan interval (date-only, and the package is scanned twice in a day) the second run COLLIDES with the first and the denominator silently loses a run. The remedy when a real file shows a scan/job id exists is one line — add it to composite_key_source. | observed_at is 'datetime' -> physical timestamptz (R5), and it is the SOURCE's inspection time, never arrival. ⚠️ crud.cast_value_by_type has NO datetime branch, so this column receives a STRING at the write boundary; PostgreSQL coerces it. Measured on assy_qa: an offset-bearing string lands correctly, garbage is REFUSED (DataError), and a NAIVE string is silently reinterpreted in the session TimeZone — which is exactly the value R5 forbids. The parser therefore emits an explicit offset and never a naive stamp. | base_x/base_y are QUANTITIES (R1 'do you do arithmetic on it') and base_wafer_id is an assigned NAME, so string (R1). stack_gate is 'number' because layer order is arithmetic and '10' < '3' lexicographically; the physical column is double precision, which cannot forbid 3.5, so the PARSER enforces integrality. | NO subject_kind column: every accepted row is package-scoped BY CONSTRUCTION (base_x is key material and the gate refuses a blank one), so the column would be a constant. NO source_file column: cell_sources.source_name already carries the originating filename per cell, and a second home for one fact is the ROOT_DEFECTS '대조 안 함' root. | NO map_key_columns: a run is not a wafer grid. Declaring them would opt this table into replace_map purge scoping and SCHEMA_CANON R3's scope-widening incident for nothing.",
    "business_key": "run_uid",
    "composite_key_source": [
      "method",
      "base_wafer_id",
      "base_x",
      "base_y",
      "stack_gate",
      "observed_at"
    ],
    "composite_key_separator": "|",
    "column_types": {
      "run_uid": "string",
      "method": "string",
      "base_wafer_id": "string",
      "base_x": "number",
      "base_y": "number",
      "stack_gate": "number",
      "recipe_id": "string",
      "eqp_id": "string",
      "observed_at": "datetime",
      "work_id": "string"
    },
    "display_columns": [
      "run_uid",
      "method",
      "base_wafer_id",
      "base_x",
      "base_y",
      "stack_gate",
      "recipe_id",
      "eqp_id",
      "observed_at",
      "work_id"
    ]
  },
  "inventory_master": {
    "__comment": "[NOT fixture data -- DO NOT DELETE AS DEAD] This table is not referenced by any fixture, so it looks unused. It is not. It exists because it is the only live exercise of the CHAIN path: test_api.py::test_chained_ingestion asserts on the outbox events the production_plan -> inventory_master chain produces, and removing these declarations silently removes that coverage. The dt_log_to_dt_map fixture chain cannot replace it -- that rule ships enabled:false on purpose (a chain can upsert map cells but cannot purge them), and turning an unsafe rule on to keep a test green is the same mistake as deleting the test. Its auto-update collector is disabled, so the table is declared but never grows.",
    "business_key": "part_no",
    "column_types": {
      "part_no": "string",
      "category": "string",
      "stock_qty": "number",
      "unit_price": "number",
      "MAX": "number",
