      "valid_from"
    ]
  },
  "wafer_process": {
    "__comment": "Per-wafer fab process history -- one row per (wafer, step). RE-DECLARED 2026-08-14; it left this file between 2026-07-28 and 2026-08-04 while its 22 rows stayed in PostgreSQL, so the table was live-but-undeclared and every consumer read it as absent: transfer_plan_config's `process_history` role reported `not_declared`, and the enrichment reference view had no dynamic model to query. The declaration below is the one from config_backup_20260801_reset, unchanged, so nothing about the shape is new. | IDENTITY IS (lot, slot), NOT wafer_id. Measured 2026-07-30: core_wafer_map.wafer_id <-> wafer_process.wafer_id matched 8 of 80, while (core_lot, core_slot) <-> (lot, slot) matched 80 of 80, and some wafer_id values are mojibake. lot/slot are therefore the join and wafer_id is a downgraded attribute. | The auto-update generator (ingestion_workspace/wafer_process/auto_update/generate_wafer_process.py, currently in auto_update_control.disabled) reads its universe from `SELECT DISTINCT core_lot, core_slot FROM bonding_log WHERE core_lot IS NOT NULL` -- an EMPTY set until 2026-08-14, which is why re-enabling it before the core columns were filled would have produced nothing.",
    "business_key": "proc_id",
    "column_types": {
      "proc_id": "string",
      "wafer_id": "string",
      "lot": "string",
      "slot": "string",
      "lot_id": "string",
